msgid "<link>Using Bookmarks</link>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: link
#. +> trunk stable
#: part.docbook:88
#, no-c-format
msgid "Automatically Wrapping Text"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: link
#. +> trunk stable
#: part.docbook:90
#, no-c-format
msgid "<link>Using automatic indenting</link>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#. +> trunk stable
#: part.docbook:96
#, no-c-format
msgid "<title>Navigating in the Text</title>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: part.docbook:98
#, no-c-format
msgid "Moving around in the text in &kate; is like in most graphical text editors. You move the cursor using the arrow keys and the <keycap>Page Up</keycap>, <keycap>Page Down</keycap>, <keycap>Home</keycap> and <keycap>End</keycap> keys in combination with the &Ctrl; and &Shift; modifiers. The &Shift; key is always used to generate a selection, while the &Ctrl; key have different effects on different keys:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: part.docbook:106
#, no-c-format
msgid "For the <keycap>Up</keycap> and <keycap>Down</keycap> keys it means scroll rather than move the cursor."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: part.docbook:108
#, no-c-format
msgid "For the <keycap>Left</keycap> and <keycap>Right</keycap> keys it means skip words rather than characters."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: part.docbook:110
#, no-c-format
msgid "for the <keycap>Page Up</keycap> and <keycap>Page Down</keycap> keys it means move to the visible edge of the view rather than browse."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: part.docbook:113
#, no-c-format
msgid "For the <keycap>Home</keycap> and <keycap>End</keycap> keys it means move to the beginning or end of the document rather than the beginning or end of the line."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: part.docbook:119
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kate; also provides you with a way to quickly jump to a matching brace or parenthese: Place the cursor on the inside of a parenthese or brace character, and press <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>6</keycap></keycombo> to jump to the matching parenthese or brace."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: part.docbook:124
#, no-c-format
msgid "In addition you can use <link linkend=\"kate-part-bookmarks\">bookmarks</link> to quickly jump to positions that you define on your own."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#. +> trunk stable
#: part.docbook:131
#, no-c-format
msgid "<title>Working with the Selection</title>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: part.docbook:133
#, no-c-format
msgid "There are two basic ways of selecting text in &kate;: using the mouse, and using the keyboard."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: part.docbook:136
#, no-c-format
msgid "To select using the mouse, hold down the &LMB; while dragging the mouse cursor from where the selection should start, to the desired end point. The text gets selected as you drag."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: part.docbook:140
#, no-c-format
msgid "Double-clicking a word will select that word."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: part.docbook:142
#, no-c-format
msgid "Triple-clicking in a line will select the entire line."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: part.docbook:144
#, no-c-format
msgid "If &Shift; is held down while clicking, text will be selected:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: part.docbook:148
#, no-c-format
msgid "If nothing is already selected, from the text cursor position to the mouse cursor position."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: part.docbook:150
#, no-c-format
msgid "If there is a selection, from and including that selection to the mouse cursor position"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: part.docbook:155
#, no-c-format
msgid "When selecting text by dragging the mouse, the selected text is copied to the clipboard, and can be pasted by clicking the middle mouse button in the editor, or in any other application to which you want to paste the text."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: part.docbook:162
#, no-c-format
msgid "To select using the keyboard, hold down the &Shift; key while using the navigation keys (Arrow keys, <keycap>Page Up</keycap>, <keycap>Page Down</keycap>, <keycap>Home</keycap> and <keycap>End</keycap>, possibly in combination with &Ctrl; to extend the move of the text cursor)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: part.docbook:168
#, no-c-format
msgid "See also the section <link linkend=\"kate-part-navigation\">Navigating in the Text</link> in this Chapter."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: part.docbook:172
#, no-c-format
msgid "To <action>Copy</action> the current selection, use the <menuchoice><guimenu>Edit</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Copy</guimenuitem></menuchoice> menu item or the keyboard shortcut (defaults to <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>C</keycap></keycombo>)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: part.docbook:178
#, no-c-format
msgid "To <action>Deselect</action> the current selection, use the <menuchoice><guimenu>Edit</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Deselect</guimenuitem></menuchoice> menu item, or the keyboard shortcut (default is <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;&Shift;<keycap>A</keycap></keycombo>), or click with the &LMB; in the editor."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#. +> trunk stable
#: part.docbook:186
#, no-c-format
msgid "Using Block Selection"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: part.docbook:188
#, no-c-format
msgid "When Block Selection is enabled, you can make <quote>vertical selections</quote> in the text, meaning selecting limited columns from multiple lines. This is handy for working with tab separated lines for example."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: part.docbook:193
#, no-c-format
msgid "Block Selection can be toggled using the <menuchoice><guimenu>Edit</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Block Selection Mode</guimenuitem></menuchoice> menu item. The default keyboard shortcut is <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;&Shift;<keycap>B</keycap> </keycombo>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#. +> trunk stable
#: part.docbook:203
#, no-c-format
msgid "Using Overwrite Selection"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: part.docbook:205
#, no-c-format
msgid "If Overwrite Selection is enabled, typing or pasting text into the selection will cause the selected text to be replaced. If not enabled, new text will be added at the position of the text cursor."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: part.docbook:210
#, no-c-format
msgid "Overwrite Selection is enabled by default."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: part.docbook:212
#, no-c-format
msgid "To change the setting for this option, use the <link linkend=\"pref-edit-cursor-selection\">Cursor &amp; Selection</link> page of the <link linkend=\"config-dialog\">Configuration Dialog</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#. +> trunk stable
#: part.docbook:220
#, no-c-format
msgid "Using Persistent Selection"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: part.docbook:222
#, no-c-format
msgid "When Persistent selection is enabled, typing characters or moving the cursor will not cause the Selection to become deselected. This means that you can move the cursor away from the selection and type text."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: part.docbook:227
#, no-c-format
msgid "Persistent Selection is disabled by default."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: part.docbook:229
#, no-c-format
msgid "Persistent Selection can be enabled in the <link linkend=\"pref-edit-cursor-selection\">Cursor &amp; Selection</link> page of the <link linkend=\"config-dialog\">Configuration Dialog</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: part.docbook:234
#, no-c-format
msgid "If Persistent Selection and Overwrite Selection are both enabled, typing or pasting text when the text cursor is inside the selection will cause it to be replaced and deselected."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#. +> trunk stable
#: part.docbook:245
#, no-c-format
msgid "<title>Copying and Pasting Text</title>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: part.docbook:247
#, no-c-format
msgid "To copy text, select it and use the <menuchoice><guimenu>Edit</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Copy</guimenuitem></menuchoice> menu item. Additionally, selecting text with the mouse will cause selected text to be copied to the X selection."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: part.docbook:253
#, no-c-format
msgid "To paste the text currently in the clipboard, use the <menuchoice> <guimenu>Edit</guimenu><guimenuitem>Paste</guimenuitem></menuchoice> menu item."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: part.docbook:258
#, no-c-format
msgid "Additionally, text selected with the mouse may be pasted by clicking the <mousebutton>middle</mousebutton> mouse button at the desired position."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: part.docbook:263
#, no-c-format
msgid "If you are using the &kde; desktop, you can retrieve earlier copied text from any application using the &klipper; icon in the system tray."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#. +> trunk stable
#: part.docbook:272
#, no-c-format
msgid "<title>Finding and Replacing Text</title>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#. +> trunk stable
#: part.docbook:275
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Search and Replace Bars"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: part.docbook:278
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kate; has an incremental search bar and a power search and replace bar, which offers the means of entering a replacement string along with a few extra options."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: part.docbook:282
#, no-c-format
msgid "The bars offer the following common options:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#. +> trunk stable
#: part.docbook:287
#, no-c-format
msgid "Find"
msgstr "Söken"

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: part.docbook:288
#, no-c-format
msgid "This is where to enter the search string. The interpretation of the string depends on some of the options described below."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#. +> trunk stable
#: part.docbook:293
#, no-c-format
msgid "Match case"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: part.docbook:295
#, no-c-format
msgid "If enabled, the search will be limited to entries that match the case (upper or lower) of each of the characters in the search pattern."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: part.docbook:302
#, no-c-format
msgid "The power search and replace bar offers some additional options:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#. +> trunk stable
#: part.docbook:308
#, no-c-format
msgid "Plain Text"
msgstr "Eenfach Text"

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: part.docbook:310
#, no-c-format
msgid "Literally match any occurrence of the search string."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#. +> trunk stable
#: part.docbook:315
#, no-c-format
msgid "Whole Words"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: part.docbook:317
#, no-c-format
msgid "If selected, the search will only match if there is a word boundary at both ends of the string matching, meaning not an alphanumeric character - either some other visible character or a line end."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#. +> trunk stable
#: part.docbook:325
#, no-c-format
msgid "Escape Sequences"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: part.docbook:327
#, no-c-format
msgid "If selected, the <guibutton>Add</guibutton> menuitem at the bottom of the context menu of the text boxes will be enabled and allows you to add escape sequences to the search pattern from a predefined list."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#. +> trunk stable
#: part.docbook:335
#, no-c-format
msgid "Regular Expression"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: part.docbook:337
#, no-c-format
msgid "If selected, the search string is interpreted as a regular expression. The <guibutton>Add</guibutton> menuitem at the bottom of the context menu of the text boxes will be enabled and allows you to add regular expression items to the search pattern from a predefined list."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: part.docbook:342
#, no-c-format
msgid "See <link linkend=\"regular-expressions\">Regular Expressions</link> for more on these."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#. +> trunk stable
#: part.docbook:348
#, no-c-format
msgid "Selection only"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: part.docbook:350
#, no-c-format
msgid "If checked, the search and replace will be performed within the selected text only."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#. +> trunk stable
#: part.docbook:356
#, no-c-format
msgid "Find all"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: part.docbook:358
#, no-c-format
msgid "Clicking this button highlights all matches in the document and shows the number of found matches in a small popup."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#. +> trunk stable
#: part.docbook:368
#, no-c-format
msgid "Finding Text"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: part.docbook:370
#, no-c-format
msgid "To find text, launch the incremental search bar with <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>F</keycap></keycombo> or from the <menuchoice><guimenu>Edit</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Find...</guimenuitem></menuchoice> menu item."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: part.docbook:374
#, no-c-format
msgid "This opens the incremental search bar at the bottom of the editor window. On the left side of the bar is an icon to close the bar, followed by a small text box for entering the search pattern."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: part.docbook:377
#, no-c-format
msgid "When you start entering characters of your search pattern, the search starts immediately. If there is a match in the text this is highlighted and the background color of the entry field changes to light green. If the search pattern does not match any string in the text, this is indicated by a light red background color of the entry field and <guilabel>Not found</guilabel> is displayed at the right side of the bar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: part.docbook:382 part.docbook:416
#, no-c-format
msgid "Use the <guilabel>Next</guilabel> or <guilabel>Previous</guilabel> button to jump to the next or previous match in the document."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: part.docbook:384
#, no-c-format
msgid "You can choose whether the search should be case sensitive. Selecting <guilabel>Match Case</guilabel> will limit finds to entries that match the case (upper or lower) of each of the characters in the search pattern."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: part.docbook:387
#, no-c-format
msgid "Click on the green arrow icon at the right side of the incremental search bar to switch to the power search and replace bar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: part.docbook:390
#, no-c-format
msgid "To repeat the last find operation, if any, without calling the incremental search bar, use <menuchoice> <shortcut><keycombo action=\"simul\"><keycap>F3</keycap></keycombo></shortcut> <guimenu>Edit</guimenu><guimenuitem>Find Next</guimenuitem></menuchoice> or <menuchoice><shortcut> <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Shift;<keycap>F3</keycap></keycombo></shortcut> <guimenu>Edit</guimenu><guimenuitem>Find Previous</guimenuitem></menuchoice>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#. +> trunk stable
#: part.docbook:404
#, no-c-format
msgid "Replacing Text"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: part.docbook:406
#, no-c-format
msgid "To replace text, launch the power search and replace bar using the <menuchoice><guimenu>Edit</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Replace</guimenuitem></menuchoice> command, or the <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>R</keycap></keycombo> shortcut."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: part.docbook:410
#, no-c-format
msgid "On the upper left side of the bar is an icon to close the bar, followed by a small text box for entering the search pattern."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: part.docbook:412
#, no-c-format
msgid "You can control the search mode by selecting the options <guilabel>Plain Text</guilabel>, <guilabel>Whole Words</guilabel>, <guilabel>Escape Sequences</guilabel> or <guilabel>Regular Expression</guilabel> described above."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: part.docbook:418
#, no-c-format
msgid "Enter the text to replace with in the text box labelled <guilabel>Replace</guilabel> and click the <guibutton>Replace</guibutton> button to replace only the highlighted text or the <guibutton>Replace All</guibutton> button to replace the search text in the whole document."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: part.docbook:422
#, no-c-format
msgid "You can modify the search and replace behaviour by selecting the different options at the bottom of the bar. Selecting <guilabel>Match Case</guilabel> will limit finds to entries that match the case (upper or lower) of each of the characters in the search pattern. <guilabel>Selection Only</guilabel> will search and replace within the current selection only. The <guilabel>Find All</guilabel> button highlights all matches in the document and shows the number of found matches in a small popup."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: part.docbook:429
#, no-c-format
msgid "Click on the green arrow icon at the right side of the power search and replace bar to switch to the incremental search bar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: part.docbook:433
#, no-c-format
msgid "If you are using a regular expression to find the text to replace, you can employ backreferences to reuse text captured in parenthesized subpatterns of the expression."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: part.docbook:435
#, no-c-format
msgid "See <xref linkend=\"regular-expressions\"/> for more on those."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: part.docbook:439
#, no-c-format
msgid "You can do <command>find</command>, <command>replace</command> and <command>ifind</command> (incremental search) from the <link linkend=\"advanced-editing-tools-commandline\">command line</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#. +> trunk stable
#: part.docbook:449
#, no-c-format
msgid "<title>Using Bookmarks</title>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: part.docbook:451
#, no-c-format
msgid "The bookmarks feature allows you to mark certain lines, to be able to easily find them again."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: part.docbook:454
#, no-c-format
msgid "You can set or remove a bookmark in a line in two ways:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: part.docbook:458
#, no-c-format
msgid "Move the insertion cursor to the line and activate the <menuchoice><guimenu>Bookmarks</guimenu><guimenuitem>Set Bookmark</guimenuitem></menuchoice> (<keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>B</keycap></keycombo>) command."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: part.docbook:464
#, no-c-format
msgid "Click in the Icon Border next to the line."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: part.docbook:469
#, no-c-format
msgid "Bookmarks are available in the <guimenu>Bookmarks</guimenu> menu. The individual bookmarks are available as menu items, labeled with the line number of the line with the bookmark, and the first few characters of the text in the line. To move the insertion cursor to the beginning of a bookmarked line, open the menu and select the bookmark."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: part.docbook:476
#, no-c-format
msgid "To quickly move between bookmarks or to the next/previous bookmark, use the <menuchoice><guimenu>Bookmarks</guimenu><guimenuitem>Next</guimenuitem> </menuchoice> (<keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl; <keycap>PgDown</keycap></keycombo>) or <menuchoice> <guimenu>Bookmarks</guimenu><guimenuitem>Previous</guimenuitem></menuchoice> (<keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>PgUp</keycap> </keycombo>) commands."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#. +> trunk stable
#: part.docbook:488
#, no-c-format
msgid "Automatically Wrapping text"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: part.docbook:490
#, no-c-format
msgid "This feature allows you to have the text formatted in a very simple way: the text will be wrapped, so that no lines exceed a maximum number of characters per line, unless there is a longer string of non-whitespace characters."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: part.docbook:494
#, no-c-format
msgid "To enable/disable it, check/uncheck the <guibutton>Static Word Wrap</guibutton> checkbox in the <link linkend=\"pref-word-wrap\">edit page</link> of the <link linkend=\"config-dialog\">configuration dialog</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: part.docbook:497
#, no-c-format
msgid "To set the maximum line width (maximum characters per line), use the <link linkend=\"pref-wrap-words-at\"><guibutton>Wrap Words At</guibutton></link> option in the <link linkend=\"pref-edit\">Editing</link> page of the <link linkend=\"config-dialog\">configuration dialog</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: part.docbook:502
#, no-c-format
msgid "If enabled, it has the following effects:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: part.docbook:506
#, no-c-format
msgid "While typing, the editor will automatically insert a hard line break after the last whitespace character at a position before the maximum line width is reached."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: part.docbook:508
#, no-c-format
msgid "While loading a document, the editor will wrap the text in a similar way, so that no lines are longer than the maximum line width, if they contain any whitespace allowing that."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: part.docbook:514
#, no-c-format
msgid "There is currently no way to set word wrap for document types, or even to enable or disable the feature on document level. This will be fixed in a future version of &kate;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#. +> trunk stable
#: part.docbook:520
#, no-c-format
msgid "<title>Using automatic indenting</title>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: part.docbook:522
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kate;s editor component supports a variation of autoindenting modes, designed for different text formats. You can pick from the available modes using the <menuchoice><guimenu>Tools</guimenu><guisubmenu>Indentation</guisubmenu></menuchoice> menu. The autoindent modules also provides a function <menuchoice><guimenu>Tools</guimenu><guimenuitem>Align</guimenuitem></menuchoice> which will recalculate the indentation of the selected or current line. Thus, you may reindent your entire document by selecting all the text and activating that action."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: part.docbook:531
#, no-c-format
msgid "All the indent modes use the indentation related settings in the active document."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk stable
#: part.docbook:534
#, no-c-format
msgid "You can set all sorts of configuration variables, including those related to indentation using <link linkend=\"config-variables\">Document Variables</link> and <link linkend=\"pref-open-save-modes-filetypes\">File types</link>."
msgstr ""

